WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.967
Republican Senator

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.801
Tommy Tuberville

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.937
is doubling down over his comments

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.105
over white nationalism

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:06.139
that he shared last night

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.574
with our Kaitlan Collins.

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:08.708
Real kept repeating

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.610
that it's just an opinion

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.513
that white nationalist are indeed racist,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.248
although the definition says so.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.983
CNN's Lauren Fox is on Capitol Hill

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.051
with the very latest.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:20.520
Lauren, what are you hearing now

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:21.221
Yeah,

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:21.921
I mean, Tuberville

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:22.889
just continues

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.991
doubling down on his comments.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.793
Originally, he made these comments

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.596
weeks ago basically arguing

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.331
that white nationalists

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:32.999
weren't necessarily racist.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:33.800
And he was pressed

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.902
repeatedly by our Kaitlan

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.270
Collins yesterday

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:37.937
and then pressed

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.407
repeatedly by reporters again today.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.875
Here's what he said.

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.578
Explain why you continue to insist

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:48.615
that white nationalists are American.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:51.284
Listen, I'm totally against racism.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.086
If the Democrats want to say

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.754
that white nationalists are racist,

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:55.955
I'm totally against that, too.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.690
But that's not a Democratic definition.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.492
The definition of a white nationalist

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.961
definition, by definition, it is racism.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:04.030
Bad and the definition. The definition.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.999
The definition is that the belief

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:08.001
that the right race is superior to

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.303
racism is totally out of the question.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.137
So do you believe that

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.306
white nationalists are racist? Yes.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.341
If that's what racism is. Yes.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.142
Thank you. But

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:20.280
And he just

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.314
continues to

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:22.649
double down in the fallout

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:24.451
on Capitol Hill from Republicans

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:25.885
is now that many Republicans

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.554
are being asked by reporters

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.789
or white nationalists racist.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.891
And I talked to several Republicans,

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.426
including Rick Scott of Florida,

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.461
who said absolutely,

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:35.895
that is the definition

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.931
of a white nationalist that they believe

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:38.965
that the white race

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.667
is superior to other races.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.969
You also heard from John Thune,

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.938
who I spoke to just moments ago.

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:46.473
He is the Republican whip

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.675
and he was pressed by reporters

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:49.209
whether or not

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:51.277
he was going to talk directly

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.879
to Thomasville about his comments.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.247
He said he had no idea

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:55.115
what Tuberville

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:57.250
was actually trying to say.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.952
He said, just to be clear, though,

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.054
there is no room for white nationalists

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.455
in the Republican Party.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.056
I pressed him

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:03.690
on whether or not

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.357
there was room

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.059
for white nationalists in the military.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:06.693
He said, no,

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:07.627
not there

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.095
either, making it clear

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.064
that he wants to put this to bed.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.233
He does not want this to become a broader

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.268
question of whether or not Republicans

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.303
are sticking with white nationalists.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:17.904
Sarah.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.072
Yeah, hard to put it to bed

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.607
when you keep getting those same answers

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:21.307
from Tuberville.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.208
Thank you so much, Lauren

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.610
Fox, for that update. Appreciate it.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.145
It's obviously not an opinion.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:27.947
It is a fact that white nationalism,

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:30.316
white nationalists are racist.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.485
Why do you think it is so hard

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.287
for Senator Tuberville

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.555
to be clear about that?

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.992
So it's interesting.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:39.626
Good to see you.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.327
But, you know, here's what's happening.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:41.995
So

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:45.398
if you listen to the full interview

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:46.566
for somebody that claims

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:47.934
to be very clear spoken,

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:48.835
and I'm just going to tell you

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.003
how I feel,

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:50.870
he is

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.105
twisting his words

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.373
around to please everybody.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:54.974
So he's trying to pretend like,

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.143
well, white nationalists are Americans

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.946
if they're racist, I'm against racism.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:00.880
But, you know,

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:01.848
it's only your opinion

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.816
that white nationalism is racism.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:04.951
So that way

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.986
he's trying to create a situation

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.388
where everybody can hear

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.789
what they want to hear,

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:12.759
because honestly, there is a constituency

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:14.027
of white nationalists

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:16.329
that you don't want to tick off, evident

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.097
in some of the Republican primaries

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.133
because they're loud on the Internet

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.467
or they have the ear of,

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.936
you know, certain people.

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.571
And so I think he is trying

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.905
to twist his words

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.207
and he does not want to.

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:28.074
It's a lot of what you saw,

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.209
frankly, with Donald Trump

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:30.443
where he didn't want to alienate

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:32.612
the proud boys and stuff like that.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.846
So it's a really,

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.348
really concerning thing.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:36.449
Let's be very clear.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.152
White nationalism is not just racism.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.920
It's deep racism.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.022
And it has no place, in my opinion,

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.857
in any political party.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.025
And it certainly has no place

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.760
in the United States military.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.930
Historically, the GOP likes to

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.566
embrace that. It is pro-military.

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.535
And the Pentagon itself has said

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.003
yes, there is a problem

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.605
with white nationalism.

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:00.807
There is a problem with extremism

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:01.774
in its ranks.

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:04.377
What does it do to the Republican Party's

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.912
historic support of the military

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:06.179
for it

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:08.214
to be home to a senator

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.016
who is saying something like this

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:12.785
by the way?

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.020
I want to be clear. It's true.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.989
There is extremism in the military.

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.090
Now, I'm not.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.691
Not necessarily at a greater rate

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.593
than all of the country,

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.794
but I've seen people like

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:22.829
I've seen

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:24.631
people tell me, I've had people tell me

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.832
QAnon theories

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.200
that are wearing the uniform

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.202
of the United States military.

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:31.571
And so, yes, we have to weed that out.

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:33.706
Just like when I joined the military,

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:35.008
I had to say

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:37.043
I am not a member of the Communist Party

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:38.077
or any party

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:38.811
or any group

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:39.779
that seeks to overturn

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.180
the United States government.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.048
And so what it does

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.183
for the historical Republican support,

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.386
they can pretend like continue to pretend

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:48.521
like they are the pro-military party

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.523
as they oppose U.S.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.592
support to Afghan or to Ukraine,

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.159
which actually

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:53.893
is preventing

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:54.961
the United States military

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:55.928
from having to get involved

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.397
directly against Russia,

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:57.697
you know,

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:58.531
as they

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.033
hold up nominations

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:00.933
because of the difference

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.702
on abortion opinion

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:05.071
and have these members of the military

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.572
that are relying on their promotions

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.641
for better pay, for better leadership,

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.209
the military that needs them

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.644
to fill these positions,

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:14.080
holding them up for politics. So, look,

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:15.782
there's plenty of

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.116
criticism that can go around

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:18.851
in terms of politicizing the military.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:20.019
In this case,

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:21.287
it is the Republicans

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:23.289
or more specifically Tommy Tuberville

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.058
that's doing exactly that.

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:28.561
So he all of this is spawning,

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:30.496
sort of spinning off of the fact

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:33.333
that he is unilaterally holding up

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.435
these military nominations

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:37.537
right over the Pentagon's abortion

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.105
leave policy.

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:40.406
How problematic is it?

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:42.308
And we're seeing this really affect,

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:43.676
right, the nomination

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:44.277
for the chairman

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:45.978
of the Joint Chiefs of Staff?

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.581
How problematic is it for Republicans

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:50.750
that this GOP senator

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.519
who cannot condemn white nationalism

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.123
as racist is holding up the nomination

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.759
of an African-American general

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:02.762
to be chairman of the Joint Chiefs

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:05.164
Well, I think it's quite problematic.

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:07.200
Now, I've kind of come to believe

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.135
that when it comes to base politics,

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:10.837
there's really nothing somebody can do

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:12.238
that's going to change the support

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:14.607
among the base unfortunately.

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:16.042
But you can chip away at it.

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:17.110
And people, I think

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.077
especially Alabama,

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.078
has got a pretty significant

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:21.147
military presence.

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:22.048
There's going to be a lot of people

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:22.982
that are actually personally

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.050
affected by this.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:24.517
Look,

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:25.885
I don't even think anybody

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:27.687
like Rand Paul,

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:29.722
who is very anti-military,

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.424
quite honestly, has taken it

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:32.759
this far before.

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:33.960
And so this is damaging

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.461
to the Republican brand.

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.929
It's damaging to Tommy Tuberville.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:40.233
So I guess he can win over some of the

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:41.834
he's probably

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:42.335
already won

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:44.103
over the anti-abortion folks,

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:45.071
but maybe he can win them

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:46.372
over even harder.

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:48.341
But even the Republicans in

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:50.343
the Senate are saying this is insane.

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:51.778
This is insane.

00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:53.780
I mean, we can't talk about competition

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:54.781
with China

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:55.648
and blame

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:56.582
President Biden

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.651
for some lack of competition with China

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:00.420
and then hold up the nominations

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.020
of the military

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.289
that is actively every day preparing for

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:04.457
hopefully not actually

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:06.159
engaging in competition

00:07:06.159 --> 00:07:07.226
or conflict with China.

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:08.661
That's the only way to prevent it.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:09.095
And Tommy

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:11.164
Tuberville is doing great damage to that.

00:07:11.164 --> 00:07:11.297
Yeah.

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:11.731
And those are

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:13.666
some of the actual nominations

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:14.934
that we're talking about, right,

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:15.935
when it comes to the Navy

00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:16.569
and the fleets

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:19.472
that are dealing with the China threat.

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:20.773
Former Congressman Adam Kinzinger,

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:21.908
thank you so much for your time.

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:22.608
We appreciate it.

